1
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,900
His fast-acting mind is one reason.

2
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,160
Wake up!

3
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:22,439
If you start napping now, it's gonna
be hard to get to sleep tonight.

4
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:27,237
There's three days of winter break left
and your homework won't finish itself.

5
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,917
Sinon finished hers before
heading back home to visit.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,717
Just saying I'm so sleepy poor thing it's
probably because the room's too warm.

7
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,777
You want me to turn down the heat?

8
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:44,797
It's not the heat it's the masters
of the sleep skill over there huh?

9
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,940
Oh well that figures.

10
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:59,777
He's been working hard on his project
ever since he got back from GGO.

11
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,897
You mean that gizmo for Yui he
demoed the other day at Egil's?

12
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,215
Oh, the mechaphonics?

13
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,220
No, it's called mechatronics.

14
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:07,840
Uh, yeah, that.

15
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,717
Anyway, he's napping
like there's no tomorrow.

16
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,630
Look at him.

17
00:01:11,713 --> 00:01:13,028
He's making me feel sleepy.

18
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:19,770
Hmm.

19
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:09,597
The story of the

20
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:12,260
beginning of the song?

21
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:15,260
The connection of the journey!

22
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:19,620
You've created the world of the future!

23
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,900
The world of the future!

24
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,030
One of the things!

25
00:02:30,113 --> 00:02:32,120
It's like a miracle!

26
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:48,840
Let's go!

27
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,310
Oh!

28
00:02:54,393 --> 00:02:56,340
Give it for my way.

29
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,160
Here you go.

30
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:08,880
Yo, guys, seriously.

31
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:12,117
Y 'all don't have to come here
every time you're on a date.

32
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,817
There's classier places
in town you could go to.

33
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,977
What are you talking about?

34
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:17,617
This place is plenty classy.

35
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:19,957
Compared to your shop in Allgate, anyway.

36
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,540
Oh, don't listen to him. I liked it.

37
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,231
That place was a rip-off.

38
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,184
Half that junk was paper mache.

39
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,515
How can you say that?

40
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,117
He was letting you stay there for free.

41
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,877
That's got nothing to do with it.

42
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,790
Oh, whatever.

43
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,002
Okay, Spill It, what's so funny?

44
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,050
Nothing.

45
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:38,440
Just, seeing you like this,

46
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:41,837
y 'all don't look anything like
the Assault Team's top players.

47
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,391
Right back at you, buddy.

48
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,660
Well, on that note, I bet you've
played MMORPGs for a long time, huh?

49
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,390
True that.

50
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,377
I played so much, I met the Mrs.

51
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:53,290
in-game.

52
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,897
She used to live in the U .S.,
and we fell for each other hard.

53
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,156
A year later, she was here,
running the place with me.

54
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:03,640
Y 'all never know what life's
got planned for you. Aww.

55
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,720
If Klein heard that story,
he'd pop a blood vessel.

56
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,433
Anyway, we got married.

57
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:13,077
Next big step was getting
ourselves a pair of NerveGear rigs.

58
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:16,219
But when the time came, we
could only pre-order one.

59
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:20,177
I remember we played some game
to see who'd get to try it first.

60
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:23,495
I'm glad it was me who cracked
the seal on it, not her.

61
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,816
Still feel that way.

62
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,137
The assault team was the only ticket out.

63
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:30,161
That's why I joined up with them.

64
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,817
All I wanted was to
get back to this place.

65
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,020
And to my lady.

66
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,317
I know what you mean.

67
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,897
I wanted to get back to my family too.

68
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,917
It's what kept me alive in there.

69
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,097
You and the assault team, brother.

70
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,137
Hell, man.

71
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:47,017
I bet every player in
Ironcrat felt the same way.

72
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,453
About going home again?

73
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,240
Right, Asuna?

74
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,305
Ain't that what motivated you?

75
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:56,880
No, not really I mean, it's
complicated between me and my family.

76
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,257
I guess that's why there
were a couple times in

77
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:03,046
there I almost forgot
what I was fighting for.

78
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,677
Sometimes I felt like I
didn't belong anywhere.

79
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,120
Real and virtual were both dead ends.

80
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,460
But then, I met Kirito.

81
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,271
He gave me something I could come home to.

82
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:20,140
A place that felt more like a home than
anything I ever had in the real world.

83
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:26,460
I was happy, even though I knew once SAO
was cleared, our cabin would be gone.

84
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,820
But I knew deep down
that one day, somehow,

85
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:32,591
I'd have a home again with Kirito and Yui.

86
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:36,840
That's what finally gave me the
strength to fight and keep fighting.

87
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,240
It gave me hope.

88
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:49,486
Speaking of Ironcrad kiddies, the mods
just posted some info on the next update.

89
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,920
It's mostly typical stuff.

90
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:55,017
They're going to be adding
new weapons and sword skills,

91
00:05:55,100 --> 00:06:00,260
but they're also going to be unlocking
floors 21 to 30 in New Aincrad. Boom.

92
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,400
Wait, do you know what that means?

93
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:09,460
If we beat the boss on floor 21, we have
a chance to buy that log cabin again.

94
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:15,160
Yeah, yeah, but there's been a ton of
little changes to New Aincrad lately.

95
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:19,365
It sucked to get our hopes up
just to find our cabins not there.

96
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:20,862
Yeah, it would.

97
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,480
But I know it's there.

98
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:25,741
It'll be waiting for us,
just like how we left it.

99
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,694
Well, y 'all better get a move on then.

100
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,964
Update goes live Christmas Eve.

101
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:59,540
Seiya, Shaul, Lindo, Ashina,
Bart, Amy, Orc Sparrow!

102
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:01,320
Ah!

103
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,500
Ah!

104
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:14,540
Ah!

105
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,050
Ah! Ah!

106
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:17,690
Ah!

107
00:07:17,773 --> 00:07:18,603
Ah!

108
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,960
Ha! Ha! Ha!

109
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,100
I'm going in!

110
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,980
Asuna, keep going.

111
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,277
I've got your back.

112
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,660
Asuna, you and me!

113
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:14,180
Watch out, Daddy!

114
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,496
It's about to punch!

115
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:18,770
Asuna, keep going.

116
00:08:18,853 --> 00:08:19,683
I've got your back.

117
00:08:19,766 --> 00:08:20,596
Asuna, you and me!

118
00:08:20,679 --> 00:08:21,509
Watch out!

119
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,330
Aisha!

120
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,360
Whoa!

121
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,100
Alright! Right!

122
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,120
We made it to floor 22!

123
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,900
Hey, Asuna!

124
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:05,077
If you're hanging around because
of the teleport gate, don't bother.

125
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,278
We can activate it.

126
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,413
Thanks a lot, you guys!

127
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,020
Are you seeing this?

128
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,480
Here we go. You ready?

129
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:34,300
Yeah!

130
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,460
I'm home.

131
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,260
Oh my God, seriously?

132
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:20,836
Hey, Asuna, wake up!

133
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,853
That goes for you, too!

134
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,857
God, would you look at that?

135
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:31,234
It's like he's daring us to stay awake.

136
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I'll make some more tea
and it'll wake us right up.

137
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,260
Hey, look!

138
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,581
I guess it stopped snowing
while we were sleeping.

139
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:44,980
Oh, have you heard the news? What?

140
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:46,860
You know, about Zek 'in.

141
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,022
Don't tell me you haven't heard.

142
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,480
Zek 'in?

143
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:53,930
Zek 'in?

144
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:58,000
Is that some kind of rare
item or something? Er, wrong.

145
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,817
It's the name of a player.

146
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,397
Actually, it's not their handle.

147
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,009
It's more like a nickname.

148
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:06,597
Anyway, this player's so badass,
someone called him Zek 'in.

149
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,777
The name caught on and there you go.

150
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:10,560
It means absolute sword.

151
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,757
Ultimate sword's better, though.

152
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,722
Either way, this player's tough.

153
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:15,930
Really?

154
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:22,200
So, uh, when did you first
hear about this second person?

155
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:23,610
I don't know.

156
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:27,397
I guess maybe the first time was
around New Year's or something.

157
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,940
Maybe a week or so ago?

158
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:30,290
Oh, duh.

159
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,757
That explains why you're so
out of the loop about it.

160
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:36,546
You've been at your family's
compound in Kyoto this whole time.

161
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,630
Mama.

162
00:12:37,713 --> 00:12:40,097
I was having a good time,
but you had to bring that up.

163
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:43,277
Listen to the rich girl
rebelling against her cushy life.

164
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,257
Sounds like a drag.

165
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:46,200
A drag is exactly what it was.

166
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:49,988
I had to sit on my knees in a
kimono all day greeting people.

167
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,220
I brought my atmosphere along,

168
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,197
thinking I could dive at night
while everyone was asleep.

169
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,339
But you know what?

170
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:00,280
The guest house I was in
didn't have Wi-Fi. Fun, right?

171
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,460
It wasn't.

172
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,360
Asuna?

173
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:35,960
Asuna?

174
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,800
You even listening? Hello? Huh?

175
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:43,177
S-sorry, I just remembered something lame.

176
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:44,737
I wonder what that could be.

177
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:46,957
Were your folks trying to
hook you up with someone?

178
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,040
No, not at all.

179
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:49,573
Forget I said anything.

180
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,160
Okay, okay, just kidding.

181
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,713
So, anyway, is this tough new
player a PKer or something?

182
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,057
Mama, just a duelist, that's all.

183
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,777
Were they in any tournaments?

184
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:01,690
Nope.

185
00:14:01,773 --> 00:14:04,177
As far as I know, this
player's a total noob.

186
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,577
I have a feeling they might have
converted over from another game, though.

187
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,157
You should see their skill stats.

188
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,005
Yes, they're through the roof.

189
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:13,040
You know how on floor 24,

190
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,877
there's that tiny little island
just north of the main town?

191
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,548
The one with the huge tree.

192
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,860
Well, every day at three o 'clock,

193
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:25,120
you-know-who shows up under that tree,
waiting to take on any challenger one-on-one.

194
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:31,597
Zekken started by posting
this opponent's wanted

195
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:34,151
notice on the MMO Tomorrow bulletin board.

196
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,640
Folks wanted to teach this
cocky ALO noobah lesson,

197
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:40,724
so on the first day, about
30 players showed up.

198
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:43,036
It didn't go so well for him, though.

199
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,840
What, they lost?

200
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:46,961
All of them, one after the other.

201
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:52,020
And get this, none of them managed to
chip off more than 30 % of Zekin's HP.

202
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,441
That's a badass.

203
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:56,820
I can't believe how good Zekken is.

204
00:14:57,420 --> 00:15:00,832
Who thought a newbie to the
game could fly as good as bad?

205
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:05,157
It took me at least six months to learn
how to fly and fight at the same time.

206
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,946
And I'm still learning stuff.

207
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:08,880
I... I did it!

208
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,760
Did you fight Zekken, too? Not even.

209
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,020
I'm no dummy.

210
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:19,217
I watched one duel and I
knew I didn't stand a chance.

211
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:22,517
If you want to know what it was like,
why don't you ask Liz and Leafa?

212
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,237
They took Zekken on yesterday.

213
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,197
They fought and lost
like a couple of champs.

214
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,397
Please don't remind me.

215
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:29,421
Good learning experience, though.

216
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,200
It's snowing.

217
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,100
Yeah, pretty, isn't it?

218
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,800
So anyway, back to Zekken.

219
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,437
If this player is as strong as you say,

220
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:47,257
it's only a matter of time before
there are no more challengers to face.

221
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:48,537
I don't know about that.

222
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,914
There's a pretty cool prize
on the line, don't you know?

223
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:53,337
Really? What is it?

224
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:55,357
Some kind of rare item or something?

225
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,146
Nope, it's nothing like that.

226
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:00,237
Whoever beats Zekken will
get an original sword skill.

227
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:03,660
It's a special move that's
supposed to be super strong.

228
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,820
An original sword skill?

229
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:08,700
What type?

230
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:09,760
How many hits?

231
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,801
Well, it's a general skill
for a one-handed sword.

232
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,657
Oh, but here's the thing.

233
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:18,100
It's an Head combo.

234
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,460
No way, 11?

235
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:25,177
The strongest original sword skill being
used right now, how many hits does it have?

236
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:28,617
That'd be the one General Eugene
developed, the Volcanic Blazer.

237
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,994
It's supposed to be an eight-hit combo.

238
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:35,180
He hasn't passed it on to anyone
else yet, and I doubt he ever will.

239
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:39,837
I guess that explains why so many players
keep lining up to challenge Zekken.

240
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:43,160
Have any of you seen this
sword skill in action? Mama.

241
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:47,377
I heard Zekken demoed it on the
first day of the duels, though.

242
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:49,813
Apparently it blew mines left and right.

243
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:54,053
But since then, it hasn't been
used in any of the fights.

244
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:56,717
Maybe the reason for
that's because there hasn't

245
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,537
been anyone tough enough
to get Zek 'in to use it.

246
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:01,740
Whoever does has my respect.

247
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:06,320
Leafa, what happened
when you fought Zek 'in?

248
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,080
Besides losing?

249
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:11,640
It was going good till
our HPs dropped below 60%.

250
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,430
But...

251
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:19,340
In the end, Zek 'in beat me,
using nothing but default skills.

252
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:20,950
Really?

253
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:24,469
Oh, I can't believe I
almost forgot to ask.

254
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,700
What's Zekon's race and
weapon of choice? An imp.

255
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:30,057
The main weapon's a one-handed sword.

256
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:33,740
It's about as skinny as your
rapier, Asuna, but only just.

257
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:36,420
And Zekon's super fast, too.

258
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:39,327
I couldn't even see the
attacks coming at me.

259
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,337
That's never happened to me before.

260
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,832
I'm still kinda shocked.

261
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,680
A speed type, huh?

262
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:49,140
If you had a hard time tracking
Zekken, I doubt I'd be able to either.

263
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,597
I know someone who might, though.

264
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,510
Mr.

265
00:17:53,593 --> 00:17:55,117
Sleepyhead's the fastest player I've seen.

266
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,553
What do you guys think?

267
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:59,309
Would Kirito go for
that kind of challenge?

268
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:01,890
What?

269
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:02,980
What'd I say?

270
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,230
Nothing.

271
00:18:05,313 --> 00:18:06,957
It's just Kazuto already tried it.

272
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:09,380
And boy, did he lose spectacularly.

273
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,200
I don't believe it.

274
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:14,516
Was he holding back?

275
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,180
Kind of hard for me to say.

276
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,217
From where I was standing,
it looked like it.

277
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:21,130
Yeah,

278
00:18:21,213 --> 00:18:25,017
but then I don't think I'm really the best
person to judge whether he was or wasn't.

279
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:28,394
He didn't use that dual-wielding
trick, that's for sure.

280
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:31,360
So I guess in a way, he
wasn't going all out.

281
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:33,759
But you know what?

282
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:36,011
That kind of makes sense.

283
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,840
I mean, it's a duel in a normal game.

284
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:43,933
There's no reason for Kitty to fight
like his life depended on it anymore.

285
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:48,885
The only time he'll take a fight seriously
now is if the game stops being a game.

286
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:51,886
when the virtual world
becomes the real world.

287
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:56,580
In a way, I hope he never goes
full tilt in a battle ever again.

288
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,662
He's kind of had enough of that.

289
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:02,607
I mean, heck, he gets into enough
trouble on his own as it is.

290
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:06,888
Yeah, I guess you're right.

291
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:12,237
Well, from where I was standing,
I got a different impression.

292
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:15,144
I think Kazuto was
definitely giving it his all.

293
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,437
He seemed serious and
focused and determined.

294
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:18,900
He put up a good fight.

295
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:22,105
At one point, though,
something weird happened.

296
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:26,473
Right before the duel was
over, they were locking swords.

297
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:29,060
And then, they both just stopped.

298
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,937
It looked like Kazuto was
saying something to Zekken.

299
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:35,902
I couldn't hear what
because of all the cheering.

300
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:40,011
And then, all of a sudden, they
backed off from each other.

301
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:45,147
Zekken charged him, but Kazuto couldn't
dodge it, and that's how the duel ended.

302
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:46,530
Really?

303
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,826
What were they talking about?

304
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:49,940
I wish I knew.

305
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:52,517
I asked him, but Kazuto wouldn't tell me.

306
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:56,217
Whatever it was, it must be pretty
important to keep to himself.

307
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,130
Interesting.

308
00:19:58,500 --> 00:19:59,382
All right then,

309
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:03,497
I guess the only way to find out
what he said is to ask Zekken myself.

310
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:06,051
Huh, you think you're up to the challenge?

311
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:08,597
I'm not doing it because
I think I can win.

312
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,856
Something about this Zekken
person intrigues me is all.

313
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:12,997
I don't know why,

314
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:17,080
but I think the second person's
here for reasons other than dueling.

315
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:19,100
Yep, that's what I think, too.

316
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:21,697
But if you want to find
out what it is, get ready,

317
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:24,517
because you're going to have to put
up as good a fight as your boy Kirito,

318
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,430
and then some.

319
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,500
Yeah, I know.

320
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,384
Will you guys come cheer me on?

321
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,697
You know we will. It'll be awesome.

322
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:34,721
We wouldn't miss it for anything.

323
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,677
Which character are
you going to duel with?

324
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,407
You still have that
Sylph account, don't you?

325
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,124
Hmm, I guess I'll use this one.

326
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,820
If Zekin's a speed type,

327
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:48,353
it'll probably come down to who can
hold out the longest, rather than DPS.

328
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,520
And that's that.

329
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:53,500
So, 3 o 'clock on the island
on Floor 24, right? Mm-hmm.

330
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:57,277
Then if we meet here
tomorrow at 2.30, we can...

331
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:59,500
Oh no, it's already 6 o 'clock!

332
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,957
We'll be late for dinner!

333
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:03,857
I guess we might as well call
it a day and log out, too.

334
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:06,411
Rich girls and their problems, am I right?

335
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,877
I can't believe he's still asleep.

336
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,717
I know, he didn't even feel a thing.

337
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,220
Hey Liz, what's up?

338
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:19,300
A little while ago, you said you
thought Zekken converted over to ALO.

339
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:25,340
The way you described the duels got me
thinking, could Zekken be someone from SAO?

340
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:34,777
Uh-huh, that's the impression
I got after my duel.

341
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:40,520
I wanted a second opinion, so after Kirito
lost his, I asked him what he thought.

342
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,840
So what did Kirito have to say?

343
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:47,137
He said that even though the
skills were through the roof,

344
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,632
Zekin's definitely not a player from SAO.

345
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:50,720
That's not all.

346
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:54,640
Kirito also said that if
Zekken really was from SAO,

347
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:57,897
the dual-wielding skill
wouldn't have gone to him.

348
00:21:57,980 --> 00:21:59,940
It would have gone to Zekken.

349
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:04,140
Kirito, Kirito,

350
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:07,060
Kirito,

351
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:08,820
Kirito, Kirito,

352
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:15,260
Kirito,

353
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:29,677
Etei.

354
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:30,800
Dying no!

355
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:37,980
Next time, Zekken.
